distributive, so $A(B-C)=AB-AC,$ but $AC\\ne CA$ because matrix multiplication is not commutative in general.\n\n- Statement III  is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $CA\\ne AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement  I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284302 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efda95f0-5dcd-5aff-a3e2-001e3cc26a43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284304} {:answer/id #uuid "8c47a968-2571-54a2-885a-ed45df9cd59c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284305} {:answer/id #uuid "fa8620b8-2e45-5c76-bbcd-a5670545d92e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284306} {:answer/id #uuid "29bb6638-1e62-5371-a72e-5100891d3700" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284307} {:answer/id #uuid "0d9fab5b-de8d-579a-b91a-92e2fa5dd08c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d9fab5b-de8d-579a-b91a-92e2fa5dd08c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284308} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb7a7b06-862d-5083-86ca-fda7c303154e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "35d12d0a-00b0-5153-a6da-b9f29bfa020a" :question/math-academy-id "q-130478" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $7\\times 7$ matrices which of the following statements are always true? \n\n- $(CA)B=C(BA)$\n- $(A+A)B=2AB$\n- $CB=BC$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I  is false. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $(CA)B=C(AB)$ is always true. However,  matrix multiplication is not commutative,   $AB\\ne BA$ in general. Therefore, $(CA)B\\ne C(BA)$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+A)B=AB+AB=2AB$ is always true.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, so $CB\\ne BC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359338 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de607e2a-211a-52fe-ba2a-cf20880ffd04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359340} {:answer/id #uuid "f578abb2-5d28-59c8-97d1-9e040b6a545e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de607e2a-211a-52fe-ba2a-cf20880ffd04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359340} :answer-field/id #uuid "a362a355-9b78-59e9-92d2-5b9079a83718" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359339} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9b8137b-d8a8-581c-9225-5d9a84d6db2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9b8137b-d8a8-581c-9225-5d9a84d6db2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359343} :answer-field/id #uuid "05cf025c-7e54-5827-bbf5-a3d7629e557c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359342} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5d2839f-7f73-50c8-9eb3-636c341cc7f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5d2839f-7f73-50c8-9eb3-636c341cc7f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359345} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0a26db9-dec6-517e-98b8-4ef077f1d24a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359344} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9002334-a340-575c-b81a-80c6764767df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9002334-a340-575c-b81a-80c6764767df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359347} :answer-field/id #uuid "48f647bc-be1d-512a-a5a2-2b4e839548cf" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "233f4ca9-b308-5f0e-8b7c-b76de566c3e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-275521" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n| $ABC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 11 \\\\ -8 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25dcc8cc-c670-5538-ae5a-f2183393a9ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25dcc8cc-c670-5538-ae5a-f2183393a9ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359350} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bfde15d-c0d4-5bd5-ab89-6a3066399132" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359349} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67e27f0c-3baf-5ac2-bf27-0a97620611a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67e27f0c-3baf-5ac2-bf27-0a97620611a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359352} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ea841dd-755f-539e-b9f4-c7f1030784c1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359351} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "406612ae-4c02-519c-9e3a-0c3529b9c23e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-182" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "406612ae-4c02-519c-9e3a-0c3529b9c23e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-182" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359354} :answer-field/id #uuid "776e12a2-58df-5d71-86df-ce9117b18ca6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359353}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "78c35ecd-2c3f-5a39-9862-6094c63c5273" :question/math-academy-id "q-319943" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $ABC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $1\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding only $1$ entry.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-20-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-26\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-26\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}78 \\\\ -52 \\\\ -182\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359355 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "daa941ab-3a21-5f8f-a3f4-232076b745df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359357} {:answer/id #uuid "8dbb1b48-4a59-5e55-975c-c2f520ff229e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359358} {:answer/id #uuid "b4439404-9021-5956-890c-dbe44584eb85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359359} {:answer/id #uuid "977243c2-3e9c-5317-b329-97876dfbbdbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359360} {:answer/id #uuid "bd698504-d416-5b02-83da-20ebeee20e4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4439404-9021-5956-890c-dbe44584eb85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359359} :answer-field/id #uuid "0eb977e5-f3bb-55d6-8615-6200132e8b34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "44d41d55-9292-54bc-9c95-2b343e22fdf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-75717" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices which of the following statements are always true? \n\n- $CB=BC$\n- $A(B-C)=AB-CA$\n- $A(BC)=(AB)C$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B-C)=AB-AC,$ but $AC\\ne CA$ because matrix multiplication is not commutative in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $A(BC)=(AB)C$ is always true.\n\nTherefore, only statement  III is true."}]}
